A top-level :REGION body is opaque payload and passes through
byte-for-byte (fmt.indent_style, issue #164). The body has keyword-shaped
lines, missing semicolons, odd spacing and blank lines; none of it may be
indented, recased, spaced or terminated, and the :region / :endregion
lines themselves are recased. (A region nested inside a procedure is left
out: range-formatting its body re-indents the body lines, an A2/A13
invariant failure reported separately.)
-- input.ssl --
:region TopLevelText;
select   a , b
  from   sample_table

:if lowercase stays
    indented line:=1
:endregion;
:PROCEDURE ReadRegion;
:DECLARE sText;
sText := GetRegion("TopLevelText");
:RETURN sText;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:REGION TopLevelText;
select   a , b
  from   sample_table

:if lowercase stays
    indented line:=1
:ENDREGION;

:PROCEDURE ReadRegion;
	:DECLARE sText;
	sText := GetRegion("TopLevelText");
	:RETURN sText;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
1:1-1:8 error keyword_uppercase: SSL keywords are case-sensitive and must be uppercase: use ':REGION'
7:1-7:11 error keyword_uppercase: SSL keywords are case-sensitive and must be uppercase: use ':ENDREGION'
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
1:1-1:8 error keyword_uppercase: SSL keywords are case-sensitive and must be uppercase: use ':REGION'
7:1-7:11 error keyword_uppercase: SSL keywords are case-sensitive and must be uppercase: use ':ENDREGION'
